# A query that starts with an operator: DS0125 says a query starts with a table.
mode: syntax
---- query
where amount > 1 | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    WHERE_OP@0..16
      IDENT@0..5 "where"
      WHITESPACE@5..6 " "
      BIN_EXPR@6..16
        NAME_REF@6..12
          IDENT@6..12 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
        GT@13..14 ">"
        WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
        LITERAL@15..16
          LONG@15..16 "1"
    WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
    PIPE@17..18 "|"
    WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
    TAKE_OP@19..25
      IDENT@19..23 "take"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      LITERAL@24..25
        LONG@24..25 "5"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0125]: a query starts with a table, not with `where`
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | where amount > 1 | take 5
  | ^^^^^ `where` is an operator
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into `where`: `'data.csv' | where amount > 1 | take 5`
